{"step_index":272,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:36:57Z","content":"All the requested adjustments have been implemented and verified. Here is a breakdown of the corrections made:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Welcome Page: Clarified Login Requirement to Verify\n- **Issue**: The secondary *\"Access Portal Dashboard\"* button on the welcome page allowed visitors to attempt entering without logging in, causing confusion.\n- **Fix**: Removed the ambiguous secondary button. The welcome page now features a single, clear, prominent action:\n  - **`[🔐 Sign In to Verify Credentials ➔]`**\n  - Clarified with explicit helper text: *\"Requires accredited Verifier, Institution Officer, or Administrator credentials.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Login Window: Centered on the Screen\n- **Issue**: The login card was aligned to the top-left corner due to missing auto-margin container styles.\n- **Fix**: \n  - Added the `.container { width: 100%; max-width: 1200px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }` rule to `style.css`.\n  - Updated `login.html` layout with a flex container (`display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: calc(100vh - 140px);`).\n  - The login card is now **centered in the middle of the screen** horizontally and vertically.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Public Cryptographic Block Stream on Welcome Page\n- Confirmed and refined the **Cryptographic Block Stream** table on the welcome page (`index.html`).\n- It remains publicly viewable on the welcome page to demonstrate proof-of-integrity and transparent SHA-256 block chaining, while keeping credential lookups secure behind authentication.\n\n---\n\n### 4. AI Verification Assistant: Fixed Hallucinations\n- **Why it was hallucinating**: The previous AI assistant had hardcoded text containing incorrect university names (*\"University of Tech & Science\"*, *\"Global Technical Institute\"*), did not dynamically look up student records like David Miller or newly issued certs, and told users to check the home page search box.\n- **Fix**: Rewrote `AiFraudDetectionService.processUserQuery()` to query the live institutional database (`qualificationRepository`) directly:\n  - *\n<truncated 652 bytes>\ntiation (Admin vs. Officer vs. Verifier)\nWe established and visually enforced distinct access tiers:\n\n| Feature / Permission | Accredited Verifier (`verifier`) | Registrar Officer (`officer`) | System Administrator (`admin`) |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Credential Verification Console** |  **Yes** (Default tab) |  **Yes** |  **Yes** |\n| **Blockchain Explorer & AI Scanner** |  **Yes** |  **Yes** |  **Yes** |\n| **Browse Student Qualifications Registry** | ❌ *Hidden / Restricted* |  **Yes** (Institutional) |  **Yes** (All Institutions) |\n| **Issue New Qualifications** | ❌ *No Issuance Rights* |  **Yes** (`+ Issue Qualification`) |  **Yes** |\n| **Revoke Qualifications** | ❌ *No Revocation Rights* | ❌ **No (Admin Only)** |  **Yes (Exclusive Authority)** |\n| **Live Server JVM Telemetry & Metrics** | ❌ *Hidden* | ❌ *Hidden* |  **Yes (Full Heap & CPU)** |\n| **System Security Audit Trail** | ❌ *Access Denied* | ❌ *Access Denied* |  **Yes (All IP & Client Logs)** |\n\n#### How This Is Displayed in the Application:\n1. **Login Page (`login.html`)**: Added a **Role Access Matrix** under each demo account button clearly listing what that role can and cannot access.\n2. **Dashboard (`dashboard.html`)**: Added an **Authenticated Session Scope Banner** displaying the user's role, badge tags, and dynamically hiding unauthorized tabs (e.g., hiding Registry and Telemetry for Verifiers; hiding Telemetry for Officers).\n3. **Qualifications Registry Table**: For Registrar Officers, the Revoke button is replaced with a locked badge: `🔒 Revoke (Admin Only)`. Only Administrators have the active red `Revoke` button.\n4. **Audit Trail (`audit.html`)**: Non-admin users attempting to view the audit trail receive an explicit *\"Access Denied: System Administrator Authorization Required\"* banner.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- Ran `mvn clean test` across the full test suite (35 unit and integration tests, Checkstyle, JaCoCo quality gates).\n- **Result**: `BUILD SUCCESS` with **0 failures, 0 errors, and 0 Checkstyle violations**.","thinking":"**Confirming Credential Verification Step**\n\nReviewing the user request, the primary goal is verification requiring a login. The initial page contained multiple access buttons. Removing the less specific button focuses the user on the clear action: logging in. The remaining button directly calls for signing in to verify credentials.\n\n\n**Centering Login and Adding Block Table**\n\nThe login screen was updated by including layout elements to center the login card on the page. The cryptographic block stream table showing mined blocks was also moved to the main welcome page for public transparency.\n\n**Fixing the AI Assistant's Verification**\n\nThe AI assistant's responses were being generated from static data and incomplete database interaction. The assistant's data retrieval was modified by directly integrating it to the database for dynamic and accurate student and certificate information, updating responses to be based on live data.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
